+# Contract: Command-Line Interface
+
+**Feature**: `001-bookmark-cli-manager` | **Date**: 2026-11-14
+
+The CLI is the tool's only external interface. This file fixes the command surface and exit
+statuses; output byte formats are in [output-formats.md](./output-formats.md); field semantics
+are in [../data-model.md](../data-model.md).
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m bookmarks [--db PATH] COMMAND [ARGS...]
+```
+
+- `src/` must be on `PYTHONPATH` (no install step — see
+  [research.md D9](../research.md#d9-tests-pytest-with-pythonpath--src-in-pyprojecttoml)).
+- `--db PATH` is a global option and precedes `COMMAND`. Omitted → `bookmarks.db` in the
+  current working directory. The file is created if absent (FR-002, FR-003).
+- `COMMAND` is one of `add`, `list`, `search`, `delete`, `export` (FR-001).
+
+## Commands
+
+### `add URL [--title TITLE] [--tags TAGS]`
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Arguments | `URL` (positional, required); `--title` (default `""`); `--tags` (comma-separated, default none) |
+| stdout on success | the new bookmark's numeric id followed by a newline, and nothing else (FR-007) |
+| Exit 0 | bookmark stored |
+| Exit 2 | `URL` does not begin with literal `http://` or `https://`; stderr names the URL and the expected prefixes; nothing stored (FR-009) |
+| Exit 1 | usage error, or store cannot be opened |
+| Notes | ids start at 1 and never repeat, including after deletions (FR-008); tags are trimmed, de-duplicated and sorted (FR-011); duplicate URLs are allowed |
+
+### `list [--tag TAG]`
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Arguments | `--tag TAG` (optional) |
+| stdout on success | one [bookmark line](./output-formats.md#bookmark-line-list-and-search) per bookmark, ascending id (FR-012, FR-015) |
+| Filtering | `--tag TAG` keeps only bookmarks carrying `TAG` as a whole tag, matched exactly and case-sensitively — `--tag doc` does not match the tag `docs` (FR-013) |
+| Exit 0 | always on success, including when nothing matches (no output) (FR-016) |
+| Exit 1 | usage error, or store cannot be opened |
+
+### `search TEXT`
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Arguments | `TEXT` (positional, required) |
+| stdout on success | one [bookmark line](./output-formats.md#bookmark-line-list-and-search) per bookmark whose **title or URL** contains `TEXT` as a substring, letter case ignored, ascending id (FR-014, FR-015) |
+| Exit 0 | always on success, including no matches (FR-016) |
+| Exit 1 | usage error, or store cannot be opened |
+| Notes | `TEXT` is matched literally — no wildcards, globbing or regular expressions |
+
+### `delete ID`
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Arguments | `ID` (positional, integer, required) |
+| stdout on success | nothing |
+| Exit 0 | bookmark removed; all other bookmarks untouched (FR-017) |
+| Exit 3 | no bookmark with that id; stderr names the missing id; nothing deleted (FR-018) |
+| Exit 1 | `ID` missing or not an integer (usage error), or store cannot be opened |
+
+### `export --format {csv,json}`
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Arguments | `--format` (required; `csv` or `json`) |
+| stdout on success | the whole collection in the requested format, ascending id — see [output-formats.md](./output-formats.md) (FR-019, FR-020) |
+| Exit 0 | export written, including for an empty store (header row only / `[]`) (FR-022) |
+| Exit 1 | any other format value, or `--format` omitted; stderr names the problem (FR-021) |
+
+## Exit statuses
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| 0 | the requested work completed (FR-005) |
+| 1 | usage error (unknown command or option, missing or malformed argument, unsupported export format) or the store could not be opened, created or read (FR-006, FR-021) |
+| 2 | `add` rejected the URL's prefix (FR-009) |
+| 3 | `delete` was given an id that is not in the store (FR-018) |
+
+Statuses 2 and 3 are reserved for exactly those two conditions; every other failure uses 1
+([research.md D5](../research.md#d5-exit-codes-2-and-3-are-reserved-so-usage-errors-exit-1)).
+
+## Stream and side-effect guarantees
+
+1. Normal results go to stdout; diagnostics go to stderr. The two are never mixed on one
+   stream.
+2. Every failure writes at least one diagnostic line to stderr naming what was wrong, and
+   writes nothing to stdout (FR-006).
+3. A failed command leaves the store byte-identical, and a failure detected before the store is
+   opened does not even create the file (FR-006, SC-007,
+   [research.md D4](../research.md#d4-validate-input-before-touching-the-store)).
+4. The tool writes nowhere except the store path the caller supplied, makes no network access,
+   and reads no configuration file or environment variable other than `PYTHONPATH`'s effect on
+   import (constitution: no hidden state).
+5. Output is encoded UTF-8 regardless of locale
+   ([research.md D7](../research.md#d7-deterministic-output-encoding)).
